          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“We were halfway through the NC500 in Scotland. The motorhome was fully loaded — camping gear, kids, dog. Then the ‘AdBlue system fault’ message appeared, followed by ‘Engine fault: repair needed.’ Then the countdown started: 700 miles before the engine would refuse to start. We limped to a garage in Inverness. The mechanic said, ‘The EGR is clogged solid with carbon. The engine is in bad shape. A replacement is going to be cheaper than trying to fix this one.’”"
        },
